{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization resolving all four main conjectures (A, B, C, D) and the Section 6 real-positivity question from Joseph Malkoun's preprint \"Finite graphs and configurations of points\" (arXiv:2508.13472v3), alongside unconditional positive theorems for linear paths LG_n and small trees. Using strictly propext, Quot.sound, and Classical.choice (zero sorry, zero admit, zero native_decide), the repository formalizes: (1) a bipartite quaternionic time-reversal Gram reduction extending Malkoun's Theorem 4.1 to all finite simple bipartite graphs (MalkounBipartite); (2) formal planar homotopy disproofs of Conjectures A, B, and Section 6 on the connected K_4-barbell B_8 (MalkounCounterexample), the 7-vertex 2-vertex-connected graph H_7 = K_4 ∪_{2e} K_3 (k4e2k3Graph in MalkounN7Counterexample; smallest counterexample found in our numerical scan — absence of connected counterexamples on n <= 6 vertices is an empirical numerical-search observation, not formally proved), and the 8-vertex triangle-free 3-regular 3-vertex-connected Wagner graph M_8 (wagnerGraph in MalkounWagnerCounterexample); (3) refutations of General Conjecture D at m=6 (rank-3 matrix on C_6) and Rank-2 Spinor Conjecture D at m=12 (2x12 Gaussian-integer witness on C_{12}) alongside unconditional Conjecture C for LG_3, LG_4, K_{1,3}, and LG_5 (MalkounConjectureD); (4) an exact planar 120-degree pinwheel zero A_{T_{10}}(x) = 0 on the 10-vertex cubic cherry tree T_{10} (cherryTree10 in MalkounConjectureC) refuting Conjecture C, tree-restricted Conjecture D, and planar tree Conjectures A and B simultaneously (absence of tree violations on 4 <= n <= 9 vertices is likewise a numerical search observation, not formally proved), plus exact integer Hopf coordinates on the 15-vertex path graph pathGraphN 15 (LG_{15}) giving Re(A_{LG_{15}}) = -40605770611892600000 / 58001564658819600000 < 0; and (5) unconditional Path Conjectures B and A (|A_{LG_n}(x)| >= 1 for all n and x in C_{LG_n}(R^3)) via an exact hyperbolic SU(2) Lyapunov transfer invariant, together with unconditional Planar Path Conjecture C (Re >= 1 for all n whenever z_u = 0) (MalkounPathPositivity). Across the 12 compared declarations in Challenge.lean, six state pure existential or negative refutations whose witnesses (B_8, C_6, C_{12}, T_{10}) reside inside Solution.lean/Matematyka/, four explicitly bind the witnesses k4e2k3Graph (Fin 7), wagnerGraph (Fin 8), cherryTree10 (Fin 10), and pathGraphN 15 (Fin 15) along with coplanarity (x.1 u 2 = 0) where advertised, and two prove unconditional path positivity for all n. Topological graph planarity of H_7, vertex-transitivity of M_8, and 50-digit mpmath companion scans lie outside the formal Lean theorems.",
